      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MALASTAR (8) has been very impressive at the trials, scoring dominantly in both outings and stamping herself as the one to beat on debut. She's done it out to 850m as well which is a big tick and she has options from the draw. Can make an impression right away. SPRINT FOR GLORY (5) trialled strongly in his only public outing, finishing in front by 0.2L in a 400m heat at Belmont. CJP's booking is a good push, as is the inside draw for a horse who showed good speed in his trial. Can sit handy and use the rail as a guide, which is a big help for these early 2YO races. ALBIREX (1) improved nicely into his second trial where he clocked a faster overall time in the process. Fiore sticking with him is a good sign and a forward showing is anticipated on debut. OCHRE (4) gets Chris Parnham on board for his debut despite not trialling him. Can play a leading role. MASQUERADE MAN (3) has trialled well coming in and ticks plenty of boxes.",
